# ClouDonna — apps/web environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in only what you need. Every variable below
# is optional — the app runs completely without this file, using the
# deterministic-only Donna Intelligence Engine (no AI provider, no network
# calls, no cost). See docs/intelligence/provider-boundaries.md and
# docs/intelligence/cost-controls.md.

# --- Donna Intelligence Engine (apps/web/src/components/donna-ai/intelligence/) ---

# Enables the OpenAI-backed narrative provider when set. Leave unset for
# local development — Donna falls back to the deterministic template
# provider automatically, with identical scores/rankings either way.
# Read ONLY by intelligence/config.ts (server-only; never sent to the
# browser). No default — there is no working key baked into this repo.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Model name passed to the OpenAI Chat Completions API.
# Default if unset: gpt-4o-mini
# DONNA_AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Milliseconds before a provider call is treated as failed and the
# deterministic fallback is used instead. Also passed as the OpenAI SDK
# client's own request timeout.
# Default if unset: 8000
# DONNA_AI_TIMEOUT_MS=8000

# Hard ceiling on generated narrative length, passed to the OpenAI API as
# max_completion_tokens.
# Default if unset: 1600
# DONNA_AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=1600

# Number of automatic retries the OpenAI SDK performs on a transient
# failure before giving up (deliberately low — a fast fallback to the
# free deterministic provider beats a slow retried request).
# Default if unset: 1
# DONNA_AI_MAX_RETRIES=1

# --- Supabase (apps/web/src/lib/supabase/, Sprint 6.1) ---
#
# All three below are optional together — leave every one unset for
# local development and the entire app runs exactly as it does today:
# no auth, no persistence, the anonymous Donna AI flow unaffected. Auth
# routes (/login, /signup, /app/*) simply have nothing to connect to
# until these are set; they do not crash the rest of the site. See
# docs/sprint-6/17-auth-implementation.md.

# Public by design — identifies the Supabase project, not a privilege.
# Every real permission is enforced by Postgres RLS, not by keeping this
# value secret. Read by src/lib/supabase/env.ts; never falls back to a
# baked-in value.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Also public by design, for the same reason as the URL above — the anon
# key is meant to be embedded in a browser bundle.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Used only to build an absolute redirect URL for magic-link/sign-up
# email confirmation (Server Actions have no request URL of their own
# to derive one from). Falls back to http://localhost:3000 if unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Deliberately NOT listed here: SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. Sprint 6.1
# introduces no service-role client — nothing in this slice needs to
# bypass RLS (every write goes through the per-request server client,
# running as the real authenticated user). See
# docs/sprint-6/08-security.md for why, if a genuine future need for one
# arises, it must never be a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable and must never be
# imported by anything reachable from a client component.

# --- Business Operations (apps/web/src/lib/inquiries/, apps/web/src/lib/notifications/) ---
#
# Both optional together. Leave unset and the inquiry system still
# works fully — inquiries persist to Supabase regardless — the only
# effect is that ConsoleNotificationProvider logs "FOUNDER EMAIL NOT
# CONFIGURED" instead of ResendNotificationProvider actually sending
# mail. See docs/operations/05-inquiry-system-v2.md.

# The address a new inquiry notification is sent to. Read by
# lib/notifications/config.ts; never hard-coded into any component.
# FOUNDER_CONTACT_EMAIL=

# Enables ResendNotificationProvider when set alongside
# FOUNDER_CONTACT_EMAIL above. Server-only — read via plain fetch()
# against Resend's API, no SDK dependency added for this one call.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
